Reflection (Week 4)
Week 4 was focused on establishing a secure and manageable server foundation. SSH key-based authentication and strict firewall rules enhance security but introduce operational constraints. Creating a non-root administrative user enforces least-privilege principles, a critical practice in professional environments.
Documenting each change and capturing evidence ensures reproducibility and allows later verification during audits.
